        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The air leakage observed during the infiltration test is not so bad. Perhaps the increase of the air sealing of the house will directly contribute to rise the efficiency of your home and maintain the heat inside the house. Also it will reduce the energy and the cost of heating.



Beside the advatages in terms of energy saving and efficiency, the fact to increse the air tightness of the house will make your home more comfortable and warm.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>The exterior walls are made from wood log which it makes a bit difficult to add insulation. But there is the possibility to add more insulation on the stucco exterior wall. If the replacement of the siding is planned it will eventually be a good idea to install more insulation. The addition of insulation from outside is recommended because it can help to seal the house properly. By insulating from outside it will not compromise or reduce the interior space.

The same procedure could be applied for the original building, but maybe it will be better to insulate from inside to keep the old fashion wood log construction and preserve the authenticity of the building.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>Accordding to the picture the insulation level of the roof is R-31, and is astimated to be R-20 in the attic of the original building. In both case there is not enough insulation. We recommend to add more insulation to reach a level of R-70.



The attic insulation play a big role in the efficiency of your home. During the heating season the insulation will block the heat and reduce the warm air to pass on the cold side in the roof and condense. The addition of insulation will help to keep the heat inside and reduce the heat loss from the roof.



On the opposite, in summer time, the insulation will reduce the heat to migrate inside the living space and overheating the  upper floor.</ceilings>
                <ceilingsCathedral />
                <foundation>The foundation walls are one of the must responsible for heat loss. Must of the heat of the house is losted by the header joist and the wall itself. When is cold outside there is a phenomen called thermal bridge that let the cold to penetrate into the living space by conduction. Therefore it is important to have a good level of insulation on the foundation walls. In this moment we estimated the insulation to be R-12. We recommend the addition of R-10,</foundation>
                <windows>At the exception of the front windows located in the basement, the rest of the windows are wood frame windows. We recommend the replacement of all windows. The windows must respect the following standards:



-ENERGY STAR

-ZONE 3

-TRIPLE GLASS

-ARGON

-LOW-E



Large windows are the biggest responsible of the sensation of cold when sitted near a window. This effect is called radiation, our body heat is absorbed by the window by radiation creating then the feeling of being cold. The suggested replacement of all windows will help to increse the air tightness of your home and make your house more comfortable.</windows>
                <doors>As we said for the windows, we recommend the replacment of the doors by ENERGY STAR doors.</doors>
                <VentilationSystem>A ventilation system would be good to increase the air quality of the house. If you are planning the installation of a ventilation system we recommend a heat recovey ventilator (HRV), certified by the Home Ventilation Institute (HVI) and certified ENERGY STAR.</VentilationSystem>
                <WaterConservation>We recommend the replacement of the existing toilet by low flow toilet. This replacement will contribute to the reduction of your water usage.



</WaterConservation>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
